        <h2>Why This Matters</h2>

        <h3>The Amplification Effect</h3>
        <p>
          When multiple AI systems cite the same AI-generated source, errors can gain an appearance of consensus and reliability. Users seeing the same information from GPT-5, Claude, and Grokipedia may assume it has been independently verified, when in fact all three may trace back to a single unverified source.
        </p>

